n# SKILL: Markdown Gold Standard for AI Trainingnn## 1. OVERVIEWnnMarkdown is not just for human readability — it is the optimal "lingua franca" for AI. Following Markdown standards helps AI:nn- **Improve context comprehension:** 40-60% better at understanding structure and meaning.n- **Save resources:** ~25% fewer tokens compared to HTML/XML or raw text.n- **Increase processing speed:** ~38% faster processing thanks to clear structure.nn## 2. STRUCTURAL RULESnn### Heading HierarchynnAI relies on headings to understand parent-child relationships and content context.nn- **REQUIRED:** Use strict logical order: `H1` -> `H2` -> `H3`.n- **FORBIDDEN:** Skip heading levels (e.g., jumping from `H1` to `H4` just for smaller text).n- **PURPOSE:** Help AI build an accurate knowledge tree.nn### Data TablesnnTables are the best way for AI to compare and extract multi-dimensional data.nn- **Requirements:** - Always include a clear header row.n  - Align columns using `|---|` syntax.n  - Do not leave cells meaninglessly blank — use "N/A" or "-" if data is missing.n- **Effect:** Helps AI perform calculations and column/row comparisons 52% more accurately.nn## 3. CONTEXT OPTIMIZATIONnn### MetadatannAlways start documents with a context information block to "activate" the appropriate knowledge domain for AI.nn**Metadata Example:**n**Document Type:** Technical Specificationn**Project:** Project Namen**Last Updated:** 2025-01-22n**Status:** Draftnn### Cross-ReferencingnnUse links to create an information network, helping AI connect discrete concepts.nn- **Syntax:** `[See Security section](#security-section)`n- **Effect:** Helps AI understand dependencies and relationships between content sections.nn## 4. DO & DON'T CHECKLISTnn| DO                                                                    | DON'T                                                                    |n| :-------------------------------------------------------------------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------- |n| Use descriptive headers that clearly describe content.                | Use formatting (bold, italic) instead of headers.                        |n| Use lists for steps or enumerations.                                  | Write process steps as long paragraphs.                                  |n| Wrap code in code blocks with language identifier (e.g., python).     | Use complex HTML/XML when unnecessary.                                   |n| Add context/metadata at the top of the file.                          | Let AI guess the document type or target audience.                       |nn## 5. GOLD STANDARD EXAMPLEnnBelow is an example of how a document should be formatted for optimal AI comprehension:nn---nn# HR Process Guide (H1)nn**Department:** HRn**Effective Date:** 01/2025nn## 1. Leave Policy (H2)nnEmployees are entitled to the following benefits based on seniority:nn| Seniority   | Leave Days   | Notes                |n| :---------- | :----------: | :------------------- |n| < 1 year    |      12      | Can be advanced      |n| > 1 year    |      15      | Non-cumulative       |nn### Leave Request Process (H3)nn1. Access the HR portal.n2. Fill out the [Leave Request Form](#leave-form).n3. Wait for approval from your direct manager.nn---n